tvfy_11062","person_slug":"sean-bell","vote":"no"},{"name":"Slade Brockman","party":"DPRES","person_id":"tvfy_10900","person_slug":"slade-brockman","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steph Hodgins-May","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_11020","person_slug":"steph-hodgins-may","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sue Lines","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10782","person_slug":"sue-lines","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Susan McDonald","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10951","person_slug":"susan-mcdonald","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tammy Tyrrell","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_11012","person_slug":"tammy-tyrrell","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tim Ayres","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10946","person_slug":"tim-ayres","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tyron Whitten","party":"One Nation","person_id":"tvfy_11060","person_slug":"tyron-whitten","vote":"no"},{"name":"Varun Ghosh","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11017","person_slug":"varun-ghosh","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Wendy Askew","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10914","person_slug":"wendy-askew","vote":"no"}],"name":"Business — Consideration of Legislation","noes":26,"question":"Claire Chandler Pursuant to contingent notice standing in the name of the Leader of the Opposition in the Senate, I move: That so much of standing orders be suspended as would prevent further considerations of the bills without a limitation of time. Let's be very clear about what is happening here. It is 1.30 pm on Thursday, and we have hit the guillotine on the most significant tax changes that we have seen in this country in a generation—rushed through a Senate inquiry process, rushed through this chamber. We have had limited time in the Committee of the Whole this afternoon to ask questions of the minister. I recognise the minister has sat here and answered questions, but we have not even been able to touch the sides on the consideration of the amendments more holistically. The Committee of the Whole is meant to be one of the most important safeguards in this chamber. It is where we examine legislation line by line, it is where we examine amendments line by line and it is where we properly test the technical detail without artificial time limits. We are a chamber of scrutiny, and this is where scrutiny actually happens. But what we are seeing today is the exact opposite of that process. As I said, this bill has been rushed from the start. It has the hallmarks of legislation that has been written in haste. And when legislation is written in haste, it demands deeper scrutiny; it does not demand less. Instead, what do we get? We get an inquiry process that can only be described as a sham. It was an inquiry where serious questions were put forward by senators: questions from stakeholders, questions about how this legislation would actually operate. Those questions were not properly answered by officials at that Senate inquiry. They were avoided. They were delayed. They were brushed aside—and I will get to what happened with the questions on notice in a moment. Now, after a rushed drafting process and an inquiry that failed to genuinely test the bill, we arrive at the","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-10352","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2026-06-25/12"}
